msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-11-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reading the animation {#reading-the-animation}"
msgstr "Membaca animasi {#reading-the-animation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Each qubit is a pie chart, one slice per Pauli type.** A qubit's marker is divided into three\n"
"slices for its $X$, $Y$ and $Z$ errors, each shaded by its own bound. This is the filtering from the\n"
"previous section built into the figure (no `pauli_filter` needed to tell the types apart).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Setiap qubit ialah carta pai, satu hirisan bagi setiap jenis Pauli.** Penanda sesuatu qubit dibahagikan kepada tiga\n"
"hirisan untuk ralat $X$, $Y$ dan $Z$nya, setiap satu dilorekkan mengikut sempadannya sendiri. Ini ialah penapisan daripada\n"
"bahagian sebelumnya yang terbina dalam rajah (tiada `pauli_filter` diperlukan untuk membezakan jenis).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Edges carry the two-qubit error bounds.** The line between two coupled qubits is shaded by the\n"
"bound on weight-2 errors acting on that pair.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tepi membawa sempadan ralat dua-qubit.** Garisan antara dua qubit yang bergandingan dilorekkan mengikut\n"
"sempadan ralat berpemberat-2 yang bertindak pada pasangan itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Light gray means no data, not a small bound.** A slice or an edge is drawn light gray when the\n"
"box's noise model has no error term for it, for instance on qubits the box does not act on. It is\n"
"drawn gray rather than dark so it cannot be confused with a bound of zero. Boxes beyond a\n"
"`max_num_boxes` limit are different: they carry the trivial bound of 2.0, so they are drawn at the\n"
"bright end of the scale.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelabu cerah bermaksud tiada data, bukan sempadan yang kecil.** Hirisan atau tepi dilukis kelabu cerah apabila\n"
"model hingar kotak tidak mempunyai terma ralat untuknya, contohnya pada qubit yang tidak dikenakan tindakan oleh kotak. Ia\n"
"dilukis kelabu dan bukan gelap supaya tidak dikelirukan dengan sempadan sifar. Kotak melebihi had\n"
"`max_num_boxes` adalah berbeza: ia membawa sempadan remeh 2.0, jadi ia dilukis pada\n"
"hujung skala yang terang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The slider steps through boxes, not through time uniformly.** There is one frame per noisy box, in\n"
"circuit order (or in reverse order with `reverse=True`, which traces the lightcone backwards from\n"
"the observable). Watching it in reverse is usually the more intuitive direction: the cone grows\n"
"outwards from the measured qubits. Each frame is labelled with its box's identifier, the same key\n"
"under which the bounds dictionary stores that box, so the slider can also be used to jump to a\n"
"particular box and look up its numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Peluncur melangkah melalui kotak, bukan melalui masa secara seragam.** Terdapat satu bingkai bagi setiap kotak berhingar, mengikut\n"
"susunan litar (atau susunan terbalik dengan `reverse=True`, yang menjejak lightcone ke belakang dari\n"
"observable). Menontonnya secara terbalik biasanya arah yang lebih intuitif: kon itu berkembang\n"
"ke luar daripada qubit yang diukur. Setiap bingkai dilabel dengan pengecam kotaknya, kunci yang sama\n"
"yang digunakan oleh kamus sempadan untuk menyimpan kotak itu, jadi peluncur juga boleh digunakan untuk melompat ke\n"
"kotak tertentu dan mencari nombornya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** The qubit layout is recovered from the coupling map's graph by embedding it into a square\n"
"lattice. A coupling map that does not embed (because it is disconnected, or too densely connected\n"
"for a grid) raises a `ValueError` rather than drawing a misleading picture.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nota:** Susun atur qubit dipulihkan daripada graf peta gandingan dengan membenamkannya ke dalam kekisi\n"
"segi empat sama. Peta gandingan yang tidak dapat dibenamkan (kerana terputus, atau terlalu padat bersambung\n"
"untuk grid) menimbulkan `ValueError` dan bukannya melukis gambar yang mengelirukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which to use {#which-to-use}"
msgstr "Yang mana satu untuk digunakan {#which-to-use}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | `draw_shaded_lightcone` | `animate_shaded_lightcone` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| geometry | the circuit diagram | the QPU coupling map |\n"
"| best for | 1D chains | any connectivity |\n"
"| Pauli types | summed, unless filtered | always split, as pie slices |\n"
"| time | all layers at once | one layer per frame |\n"
"| output | a `matplotlib` figure | a `plotly` figure |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | `draw_shaded_lightcone` | `animate_shaded_lightcone` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| geometri | rajah litar | peta gandingan QPU |\n"
"| terbaik untuk | rantai 1D | sebarang kesambungan |\n"
"| jenis Pauli | dijumlahkan, melainkan ditapis | sentiasa dipisahkan, sebagai hirisan pai |\n"
"| masa | semua lapisan serentak | satu lapisan setiap bingkai |\n"
"| output | rajah `matplotlib` | rajah `plotly` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a 1D chain the static figure is easier to take in at a glance and reproduces in a paper. Beyond\n"
"1D the animation is the only one of the two that shows the spatial structure faithfully.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk rantai 1D, rajah statik lebih mudah ditangkap sepintas lalu dan boleh dihasilkan semula dalam kertas kerja. Di luar\n"
"1D, animasi ialah satu-satunya daripada kedua-duanya yang menunjukkan struktur ruang dengan setia.\n"
